Principle 1

Simple > Clever

Readable code wins.

Principle 2

No duplicated business logic

Harvest calculations should live in one place.

Principle 3

Everything important is typed

Avoid any unless there's a compelling reason.

Principle 4

Every API has one clear responsibility

Keep endpoints focused and predictable.

Principle 5

UI components should be composable

Build Lego bricks, not monoliths.

Principle 6

Database is the source of truth

Never rely on frontend calculations for business rules.

Principle 7

Optimize for maintainability

This project may eventually have tens of thousands of farms. Decisions should support that future.

One thing I'd like to be responsible for

I think we should have an "Architecture Review" at the end of every few milestones.

Not a product review.

A technical review.

Questions like:

Is the folder structure still healthy?
Are services getting too large?
Do we need caching yet?
Are we introducing duplicate models?
Should this become an event instead of a synchronous call?
Is the API still coherent?
Where is technical debt accumulating?

Those reviews prevent the project from slowly becoming difficult to work on.